My understanding is that the issue is happening here:

`/ArduPlane/altitude.cpp:L271`

```
int32_t relative_alt = target_altitude.amsl_cm - home.alt;
    relative_alt += mission_alt_offset()*100;
```

Where in auto mode, you have home.alt to say, 100m, and it has already reached the altitude with the offset. Assume you're using ALT_OFFSET = 300m, then, once you set a new guided waypoint, it seems like you're setting the "target_loc" to the new altitude (400m), but in reality, you want the to set the altitude of this new waypoint at what auto mode is _without_ the offset: (i.e 100). Then you should see that the guided waypoint will leave you at the "correct" new waypoint altitude (100m + OFFSET = 400).

This code is responsible for setting the target_loc in the `ModeGuided` is here:

`ArduPlane/mode_guided.cpp:L109`
```
bool ModeGuided::handle_guided_request(Location target_loc)
{
    plane.fix_terrain_WP(target_loc, __LINE__);
    // add home alt if needed
    if (!target_loc.terrain_alt) {
        target_loc.change_alt_frame(Location::AltFrame::ABSOLUTE);
    }

    plane.set_guided_WP(target_loc);

    return true;
}
```

It's not really clear if this is more of a "UI" bug or a backend bug. It seems like the intended behaviour was to have the home.alt propagate through so it's not really clear to me how to "fix" it in a reliable manner.

