You can however set the serial protocol to mavlink2 and configure the GM (using the GM application from the vendor) with the RC channels that you are using to control pitch, yaw (and roll) as well as the gimbal mode.  ( think this is what @andrewkena was referring to).  Note that I could not get this working very well and the movement had lag by close to a second with the commanded movement.  I think this is related to my ELRS setup and control frequency.

What is needed in the ardu config is to be able to select the gimbal mode to lock the 3 gimbal axis to the craft as the gimbal defaults to self levelling mode and is NOT suited (high risk) to flying as FPV. (see: https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/issues/30640)

[Mode::get_alt_above_ground_cm() ](https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/mode.cpp#L603) strangely checks whether the position controller is active or not and if NOT active (e.g. the vehicle is in AltHold, pilot-controlled-Land, Stabilize or Acro mode) it returns the alt-above-home instead of the alt-above-terrain.

This function is used in these places:

- weather vaning (weather vaning is disabled at low altitudes)
- landing gear may be raised or lowered
- LAND mode vertical speed (including Land-within-RTL, Land-within-Auto)

I think this bad behaviour could happen:

1. If the EKF failsafe triggers and the vehicle switches to Land mode (using pilot control), the vehicle may not slow to LAND_SPEED at too high an altitude or not at all.  This means it could drift far further than it should or it could hit the ground at 1.5m/s instead of 0.5 m/s.  The landing gear might also not be deployed before touchdown
2. Landing gear could lower and retract as the user switches between Loiter mode and AltHold mode
3. Weather vaning might be enabled/disabled at the wrong altitude

My guess is that we can just remove this position controller check but we should also test the above scenarios to confirm they really do happen before the change and don't afterwards.

Below is the current code for easy reference

```
/*
  get a height above ground estimate for landing
 */
int32_t Mode::get_alt_above_ground_cm(void) const
{
    int32_t alt_above_ground_cm;
    if (copter.get_rangefinder_height_interpolated_cm(alt_above_ground_cm)) {
        return alt_above_ground_cm;
    }
    if (!pos_control->is_active_NE()) {
        return copter.current_loc.alt;
    }
    if (copter.current_loc.get_alt_cm(Location::AltFrame::ABOVE_TERRAIN, alt_above_ground_cm)) {
        return alt_above_ground_cm;
    }

    // Assume the Earth is flat:
    return copter.current_loc.alt;
}
```

