@pavloblindnology there are various submodes in guided which don't even require an EKF origin be set - SubMode::Angle, for example.  So I don't think we can institute blanket checks as you suggest.

We should probably change things around so that we can fail to enter submodes within guided based on what condition the vehicle is in.  So, for example, to enter wpnav mode you'd need to be able to get an absolute position from the AHRS.  To enter VelAccel mode you would need to be able to get a velocity from the AHRS (eg. via OpticalFlow).  Local position commands would require EKF origin be set to be accepted.

The advantage of this is that we can remove the requirement of disabling GPS checks when you want to work with OpticalFlow.

