I have looked over the concept of shutting down the harmonic notch. Tridge suggested ramping the attenuation. This appears to be a good approach and can done without the conversion from dB. The key is we should ensure that the phase lag does not increase above that of the lowest frequency setting to ensure we don't cause existing aircraft to oscillate. The narrower the notch, the faster we must shut it down to do this.

0.01 bandwidth ratio:
![image](https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/assets/100896/035e7be9-8b1f-4e39-a72a-7aac5d761d1e)

0.1 bandwidth ratio:
![image](https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/assets/100896/ffc462d2-d3c8-41b3-a8a2-34c1c440254f)

0.5 bandwidth ratio:
![image](https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/assets/100896/af4e9116-94b5-4c3e-bb95-5d7ba21e5138)

For these graphs I used:

`
sampleRate_Hz = 1000;
filterFreq_Hz =20;
BWR = 0.5;
bandwidth_Hz = filterFreq_Hz * BWR;

Ref = 0.0:0.1:1;
A = sqrt(Ref);
filterFreq_Hz = filterFreq_Hz * (1-BWR + BWR * Ref(end👎1));`

I found the sqrt(Ref) worked well to keep the phase lag under the min frequency setting.

I would not want the notch to stay on below half the cut off though so we would need to add some code to do this for bandwidths above 50%.

We must do this referenced to the expected noise frequency freq_exp_Hz, our minimum frequency freq_min_Hz, bandwidth bandwidth_Hz, and attenuation A (after conversion from dB).

```
ref = constrain_float( ( freq_min_Hz - freq_exp_Hz ) / bandwidth_Hz, 0.0f, 1.0);
A_new = A * (1.0 - ref) + ref * sqrt(ref);
```

as freq_exp_Hz moves below freq_min_Hz towards freq_min_Hz - bandwidth_Hz, ref moves from 0.0 to 1.0
as ref moves from 0.0 to 1.0, A_new moves from A to 1.0.

When A_new = 1 the notch is a direct pass through with no phase delay for all values of centre frequency.

Now we also need to ensure we don't ever go below half the minimum frequency. So we may need to extend this a little.

```
bandwidth_ref_Hz = MIN(freq_exp_Hz / 2, bandwidth_Hz);
ref = constrain_float( ( freq_min_Hz - freq_exp_Hz ) / bandwidth_ref_Hz, 0.0f, 1.0);
A_new = sqrt( A^2 * (1.0 - ref) + ref);
```

