```
void ekf_imu_buffer::push_youngest_element(const void *element)
{
    if (!buffer) {
        INTERNAL_ERROR(AP_InternalError::error_t::flow_of_control);
        return;
    }
    // push youngest to the buffer
    _youngest = (_youngest+1) % _size;
    memcpy(get_offset(_youngest), element, elsize);
    // set oldest data index
    _oldest = (_youngest+1) % _size;
    if (_oldest == 0) {                    // <=============BUG!!!
        _filled = true;
    }
}
```
, I think 
```
    if (_oldest == 0) {
        _filled = true;
    }
```
should be modified as:
```
    if (_oldest == 1 || _size == 1) {
        _filled = true;
    }
```

Why?

because when push, the first element is pushed into pos 1 NOT pos 2:
```
_youngest = (_youngest+1) % _size;  // here _youngest is initialized as 0, so the first elem pos is 1 not 0
```

so when _oldest is 0, there is N-1 elem not N elem in buffer:
` _oldest = (_youngest+1) % _size;` 
